# Pachelbel, Canon in D, complete first-violin line (57 bars), reduced for piano
# over the original two-bar ground bass. Violin II and III, which imitate the
# same theme at two-bar intervals, are NOT included; this is NOT the full
# three-violin score or a modern keyboard arrangement.
# The opening is checked against the 1838-42 manuscript (Berlin Mus.ms. 16481/8),
# preserving the first eight bars previously transcribed in InHarmonia.
# Continuation follows Michael Fischer v. Mollard's full first-violin transcription,
# Mutopia Project (2015), CC BY 4.0, based on IMSLP:
# https://github.com/MutopiaProject/MutopiaProject/tree/master/ftp/PachelbelJ/Canon_per_3_Violini_e_Basso
# https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
# Changes: monophonic first violin moved to piano RH; repeated ground bass in LH;
# harmonic chord symbols supplied by InHarmonia; no other violin parts or figured
# continuo realizations; no additional compositional notes.
title: Canon in D
piece: canon-in-d
added: 2026-10-17
source: public-domain
composer: Johann Pachelbel
composer-died: 1706
first-published: 1919
edition: Manuscript ca. 1838-42, Staatsbibliothek zu Berlin, Mus.ms. 16481/8 (IMSLP #346264); full violin I transcription Michael Fischer v. Mollard, Mutopia Project 2015, CC BY 4.0
key: D major
meter: 4/4
# Tempo is editorial; the manuscript gives none.
tempo: 64
summary: Full first-violin canon across 57 bars over Pachelbel's repeating ground bass (piano reduction; other violins omitted).
figure: held
medium-figure: held
# Retain the characteristic opening arpeggios in Easy; fast variations elsewhere
# are simplified by the generator without altering the source.
easy-keep: 5, 6

[Ground] 1-2
melody: | r:4 | r:4 |
chords: | D A Bm F#m | G D G A |
left: | D3q A2 B2 F#2 | G2q D2 G2 A2 |

